  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Papua New Guinea Kokoda Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kokoda Initiative Partnership (KIP) is one of three place-based program components under the INN928 Australia-PNG Subnational Program. KIP is the program through which Australia funds its obligations under the Kokoda Initiative (KI), an enduring partnership between PNG and Australia to protect the Owen Stanley Ranges and the Brown River catchment. The program is organised under three pillars (the Track, the People, and the Environment) and focuses on preservation of military, cultural and environmental values of the broader Kokoda catchment region, as well as improving local communities&#x2019; access to economic livelihood opportunities, health, education, gender equality, disability and social inclusion. This will be achieved by taking a locally led development approach and partnering closely with the provincial government, local communities and development actors.</narrative>
  </description>
